 the  week and not tell you but as I did  earlier today as and is demonetized  that Fox News is parroting talking  points literally from the shooters  manifesto or talking about Donald  Trump's reactions to the shooting or  talking about Republican elected  officials blaming video games I could  choose not to cover it fully but that  would be the wrong  and so what happened is that on Monday  we had three videos related to the  shootings and all three videos were  demonetized  yesterday there was more work to do  there was more follow-up to do and  literally half of the videos we  published yesterday three of the six as  I'm showing on screen right now were  demonetized some of them got a ton of  views on which we made no money it's a  video here and a video there but when  you look at the views because these  videos did well which is important  because that means that people actually  care about this stuff  this week just from Monday and Tuesday  we had 350,000 views on these few Clips  demonetised completely so there are a  few things at play here first  it's the advertisers that drive this  it's not it's easy to blame YouTube and  of course YouTube is complicit in the  system it's not YouTube's fault per se  advertisers impose restrictions on  YouTube particularly since the panic of  ad pocalypse 2017 and YouTube wants to  placate them because YouTube is a  for-profit company so they say anything  remotely controversial related to crime  or violence or terrorism we will not run  ads on we will cater to you advertisers  is what YouTube effectively says not the  creators of course and in a way not to  the audience either because in some way  shape or form not everybody can do what  we do which is to say screw the  monetization I'm going to cover what's  important there are creators that either  choose to or are sort of forced into for  financial reasons  staying away from topics that they know  are going to be d monetized and in a way  it's so childish it's quite similar to  censorship in television with regard to  swear words and sexual situations in  other countries like my home country of  Argentina this is like no big deal you  know swearing on TV is not really a big  deal in many countries it's much more  common that when you're watching serious  news reports about bad things that  happen even what is shown is far less  sanitized and more graphic we can talk  about the impact on children or whatever  else that's a perfectly legitimate  conversation but in the United States  adults in many cases are not just  treated like adults when it comes to  media restrictions so that's number one  secondly this goes to the bigger problem  as I've been saying of the connection  between monetization of content and the  desires of advertisers that is  systemically a connection that is  problematic and so that's why you know I  really really really appreciate the  people that understand the sort of  urgency and destructive nature of that  status quo and have stepped up in the  last couple of months and funded us  directly as this problem has gotten  bigger and bigger on YouTube we had a  record record all-time record new  membership month in June awesome July  fell slightly short of that but July  became our second best month ever for  new supporters August is off to a good  enough start that maybe it'll come in  sort of around July right around second  best and the amazing thing is people  seem to be getting it and it could not  be happening at a more important time  membership culture supporting what you  believe in this is the path forward  there are easy ways to do it with our  show but you don't have to do it with  our show do it with whatever show is  important to you okay  membership this takes a minute david  pakman.com slash membership coupon codes  are available this is 20/20 saves you  40% I'll even give you a crazier coupon  code this one I usually don't mention  except in very specific situations the  coupon code half 19h A